From ebbbe6a54077d3d509401f44bf1b1660983895f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Manzano <leftspin@me.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:03:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] screencast: don't destroy the process retry timer twice

xdpw_screencast_instance_destroy() destroys every timer owned by the
cast, including process_retry, but leaves the pointer set. Destroying
the stream afterwards pauses it, and the state change handler destroys
process_retry again: a use-after-free that crashes xdpw when a session
closes while the stream is starved of buffers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/screencast/screencast.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/screencast/screencast.c b/src/screencast/screencast.c
index a8fdc10..d9dc52f 100644
--- a/src/screencast/screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/screencast.c
@@ -93,6 +93,9 @@ void xdpw_screencast_instance_destroy(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 			xdpw_destroy_timer(timer);
 		}
 	}
+	// Destroyed above, the stream state change on disconnect must not
+	// destroy it again
+	cast->process_retry = NULL;
 	struct xdpw_session *sess, *stmp;
 	wl_list_for_each_safe(sess, stmp, &cast->ctx->state->xdpw_sessions, link) {
 		if (sess->screencast_data.screencast_instance == cast) {
-- 
